        <body>
            <div xml:id="d59-a1-a3">

                <pb facs="0136" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg94"/>

                <head>Surrey Resolutions.</head>
                <opener>
                    <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Heath House, Weybridge, Surrey, and
                            Chamber of London</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Guildhall, E.
                        C.</hi>,</placeName> 1863.</opener>
                <p>At a public meeting of the inhabitants of Cobham, in the county of Surrey, held
                    in the Wesleyan church, on January 16, 1863, it was—</p>
                <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">Resolved, unanimously</hi>, That this meeting, being
                    convinced that slavery is the cause of the grievous civil war now being waged in
                    America, and that the object of the leaders of the rebellion in that country is
                    the perpetuation and extension of that inhuman system, earnestly prays that the
                    United States government may be strengthened to pursue its emancipation policy
                    till not a slave shall be left on American soil.</p>
                <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">Resolved</hi>, That a copy of this resolution be
                    forwarded to Mr. Abraham Lincoln, President of the United States.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>BENJAMIN SCOTT, <hi rendition="#italic">Chairman</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
